// Cs13.grammar — C# 13.0: field keyword (T3.13.1).
//
// The `field` keyword refers to the backing field of an auto-property and can be used in the
// getter/setter body:
//   class MyClass {
//       public int Value {
//           get => field;
//           set => field = value;
//       }
//   }
//
// Roslyn refs (C:\RSDN\roslyn, main, src/Compilers/CSharp/Portable):
//   * SyntaxKind.FieldKeyword = 8412 (Syntax/SyntaxKind.cs:349).
//   * FieldExpressionSyntax — a single-token node for the `field` keyword
//     (Generated/CSharpSyntaxGenerator/.../Syntax.xml.Main.Generated.cs:3015:
//     `SyntaxFactory.FieldExpression(SyntaxFactory.Token(SyntaxKind.FieldKeyword))`).
//   * Parsed in primary-expression position — ParsePrimaryExpressionWithoutPostfix
//     (Parser/LanguageParser.cs:12009-12012): `else if (IsCurrentTokenFieldInKeywordContext() &&
//     PeekToken(1).Kind != SyntaxKind.ColonColonToken) return _syntaxFactory.FieldExpression(
//     this.EatContextualToken(SyntaxKind.FieldKeyword));`
//   * IsCurrentTokenFieldInKeywordContext (Parser/LanguageParser.cs:6097-6102):
//     `CurrentToken.ContextualKind == SyntaxKind.FieldKeyword && IsInFieldKeywordContext &&
//     IsFeatureEnabled(MessageID.IDS_FeatureFieldKeyword)`.
//   * The field-keyword context (IsInFieldKeywordContext) is set in the property accessor body via
//     ParserSyntaxContextResetter (Parser/LanguageParser.cs:4286, 4639).
//   * Version gate — `field` is a C# 13.0 feature (MessageID.IDS_FeatureFieldKeyword,
//     MessageID.cs:290; binder check Binder_Expressions.cs:1572). The PARSER accepts the form wherever
//     the rule exists; version purity comes from the rules being Cs13-only.
//
// APPROACH (three parts):
//   1. FieldExpression primary — re-declares Primary (append, T0.3 merge) to add `field` as a primary
//      expression (the backing-field reference). Roslyn FieldExpression (LanguageParser.cs:12009-12012).
//   2. `field` reservation — re-declares ReservedKeyword (append) to reserve `field` at v13, so a bare
//      `field` in expression position is NOT a plain IdentifierName; the FieldExpr primary is the SOLE
//      match (no equal-length tie).
//   3. Expression-bodied accessors — re-declares Property (append) with an alternative that uses
//      ExpressionBodiedAccessorList (`get => Expr ;` / `set => Expr ;`). The `=>` accessor form is the
//      REQUIRED-new-construct, mutually exclusive with the Cs1 (block, AccessorDeclaration+) and Cs3
//      (auto, AutoPropertyAccessorList) Property alternatives — the token after the accessor name
//      disambiguates (`{` vs `;` vs `=>`) — no equal-length tie.
//
// CS13 only: at v<=12 the FieldExpr primary, the `field` reservation, and the `=>` accessor alternative
// are ABSENT, so `get => field;` / `set => field = value;` match no Property alternative and REJECT.
//
// Boundary / deviation: reserving `field` at v13 (not at v<=12) means a bare identifier use
// (`int field;`) is accepted at v<=12 but rejected at v13 — a documented deviation from Roslyn (where
// `field` is a contextual keyword valid as an identifier at every version). The task's version-purity
// requirement (the `field` KEYWORD in an accessor body) is satisfied: `get => field;` is rejected at v12
// (no `=>` accessor) and accepted at v13.

// === FieldExpression (C# 13.0, T3.13.1). ===
// The `field` keyword as a primary expression — the backing-field reference in a property accessor
// body. Roslyn ParsePrimaryExpressionWithoutPostfix (LanguageParser.cs:12009-12012) +
// IsCurrentTokenFieldInKeywordContext (6097-6102). Re-declares Primary (append, T0.3 merge).
// `field` is reserved (below), so IdentifierName (`!ReservedKeyword Identifier`) does NOT match it;
// FieldExpr is the SOLE Primary match for `field` -> no equal-length tie.
Primary =
    | FieldExpr = "field";

// === `field` reservation (version-purity, Cs13-only). ===
// Re-declares ReservedKeyword (append) to reserve `field` at v13. This makes `field` NOT a valid
// IdentifierName at v13, so the FieldExpr primary (above) is the sole match for `field` in expression
// position. At v<=12 `field` is not reserved (a valid identifier), but the `=>` accessor form is absent,
// so `get => field;` REJECTS anyway.
ReservedKeyword =
    | "field";

// === Expression-bodied accessors (C# 13.0, T3.13.1). ===
// Re-declares Property (append, T0.3 merge) with an alternative that REQUIRES expression-bodied (`=>`)
// accessors via ExpressionBodiedAccessorList. Mutually exclusive with the Cs1 (block, AccessorDeclaration+)
// and Cs3 (auto, AutoPropertyAccessorList) Property alternatives — the token after the accessor name
// disambiguates (`{` vs `;` vs `=>`) — no equal-length tie. The body is a full TDOPP expression, so
// `field = value` parses as an assignment.
Property = Attributes? PropertyModifier* Type TypeName "{" ExpressionBodiedAccessorList "}" ";"?;

// Expression-bodied accessor list: `get => Expr ;` and/or `set => Expr ;`. Named union (the
// meta-grammar forbids `|` inside a group). The two shapes are disambiguated by longest-match (a longer
// shape wins); none has an equal-length tie with another (each differs in a leading token).
ExpressionBodiedAccessorList =
    | ExprGetterOnly = "get" "=>" Expression ";"
    | ExprGetSet = "get" "=>" Expression ";" "set" "=>" Expression ";";

// === Event field (C# 13.0, T3.13.2). ===
// An event field is an event declaration with an initializer (like a field):
//   public event Action MyEvent = () => { };
// Roslyn: ParseEventDeclaration (LanguageParser.cs:5082-5095) -> IsFieldDeclaration (3429-3468) ->
// ParseEventFieldDeclaration (5222-5255): `event` + Type + name + `= Expression` + `;`
// (EventFieldDeclarationSyntax, Syntax.xml.Syntax.Generated.cs:12407; SyntaxKind.EventFieldDeclaration
// = 8874, SyntaxKind.cs:827). The `= Expression` initializer is the C# 13.0 addition (MessageID
// IDS_FeatureEventFields). Re-declares EventTail (append, T0.3 merge): the Cs1 Event (Cs1.grammar:429)
// references EventTail, so it picks up this third tail form automatically. The three EventTail
// alternatives are mutually exclusive by leading token (`;` vs `{` vs `=`) -> no equal-length tie.
// CS13 only: at v<=12 the `= Expression ;` tail is absent, so `event ... = ...;` matches no EventTail
// -> the Event rule fails -> REJECT.
EventTail =
    | EventFieldInit = "=" Expression ";";
